id: pm-5y05kq
title: "The output encoding named toon has no tabular array form, so every row collection pays three to five lines per row while the storage format beside it uses the encoding correctly"
description: "Item files on disk use real TOON: a length-marked tabular header followed by CSV rows (a dependencies block with an explicit row count and column list, tags with a length marker). The renderer behind --output-format toon in the output module has no tabular branch at all - arrays of uniform flat objects render as YAML-style expanded blocks, one line per field per row, with no length marker anywhere. Measured on the live tracker: activity rows 2046 bytes expanded versus 1307 tabular (36 percent smaller), list rows 3948 versus 3074 (22 percent), next rows 2062 versus 1405 (32 percent). The cost is paid by every read command that returns a row collection, and an agent that learned the tabular encoding from item files cannot reuse that knowledge on command output. This is the encoding half of the same waste that the row-contract suppression item measures on the envelope half."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,context-efficiency,output-contracts,token-budget,toon
created_at: "2026-08-11T05:24:19.788Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T09:18:21.849Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#f016837593b4e6bc7293988d"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The toon renderer emits a length-marked tabular header plus CSV rows for arrays whose entries are flat objects sharing one key set, and falls back to the current expanded form for every other shape; Values containing a separator, a quote or a newline are quoted and escaped so a rendered tabular row round-trips through the existing toon decoder; The active row encoding is discoverable from the output contract or its replacement, so agents parse tabular and expanded output without guessing; The per-command saving is measured in the token-budget-gate corpus and declared as a ratchet floor rather than recorded as a one-time improvement; The json encoding is unchanged and existing snapshot fixtures are regenerated in the same change"
parent: pm-5t33or
